Everpure (NYSE: P) has evolved from storage pioneer to data platform, closing fiscal 2026 with $3.7 billion in revenue, its first billion-dollar quarter, and accelerating growth into FY27. Our strategic agenda spans the companies defining the next era of technology - hyperscalers, AI labs, the AI hardware supply chain, data platform providers, and the broader AI ecosystem.

This type of work-work that changes the world-is what the tech industry was founded on. So, if you're ready to seize the endless opportunities and leave your mark, come join us.

THE ROLE

As an Everpure Hardware Engineer focused on DRAM, you will work with some of the best engineering teams and leaders in the industry. You will own the relationship with suppliers from the engineering side, work with other engineering leads on driving the best RAS capability for DRAM,&nbsp; own DRAM validation from a systems perspective for both new and existing products while continuously improving validation methodologies to ensure best-in-class quality and reliability.

In this role, you will stay current with the latest product roadmap, supplier relationships, industry trends, and latest validations tools. You will work with the latest x86 and ARM based CPUs, align with SW teams to drive the latest BIOS and microcode across products.&nbsp; This position works with all the HW teams at Everpure, so you will be the resident expert and go to person for all DRAM related items.&nbsp; This role is part of the HW team so it allows the engineer to delve into other System level validation and design opportunities.

WHAT YOU'LL DO

• Defining test plans and validation for DIMMs from a system perspective&nbsp;

• Performing hands-on lab characterization of DIMM Modules and interfaces&nbsp;

•

• Running stress tests to characterize signal integrity&nbsp;

• Injecting errors to characterize correct behaviour&nbsp;

• Using oscilloscopes and logic analyzers as necessary for validation and debug&nbsp;

• Understanding and ability to debug serial and management busses as necessary&nbsp;&nbsp;

• Writing clear validation reports and communicating results to cross-functional engineering teams, including hardware, software, and operations

• Though the position focuses on DRAM driving peripheral qualification efforts, other technologies on the motherboard maybe required including:

•

• DRAM

• x86/ARM CPUs

• PCIe&nbsp;

• Owning and reporting field and manufacturing statistics across various DIMM vendors&nbsp;

• Driving reporting of operations and factory data&nbsp;

• Working with RAS architects and helping drive error handling strategy&nbsp;

• Working across all Everpure products and driving alignment of BIOS as it pertains to DIMMs&nbsp;

• Supporting reviews of hardware designs and JDM validation reports, and assisting software and diagnostics engineering with lab debug

• Owning products from cradle to grave, including reviewing field failures, driving down failure rates, and performing root cause analysis on abnormalities

• We are primarily an in-office environment and therefore, you will be expected to work from the Santa Clara office in compliance with Everpure's policies, unless you are on PTO, or work travel, or other approved leave.

WHAT YOU BRING

• 7+ years of experience&nbsp;

• Bachelor or Masters in Electrical Engineering

• Strong knowledge of the areas listed above and excellent debug skills

• Familiarity with fleet-scale hardware fault management strategies that maintain system resilience in the presence of DRAM failures.

• Strong scripting skills in Python, Bash, Linux, or similar environments

• Proficiency with spreadsheets SQL, and experience visualizing data

• Excellent communication skills with strong execution and schedule discipline

• Solid experience using Jira and other bug-tracking tools

• Experience working with lab debug tools oscilloscopes, logic analyzers, etc

• Experience working with 3rd party suppliers and driving relationships and roadmaps

Grau de Instrução

Grau de instrução: Pós Graduação;

Formação: Ensino superior completo, com formação em engenharia e pós graduação em engenharia de segurança do trabalho, com registro no CREA.

Tempo de Experiência:

Experiencia em atividades correlatas ao escopo do serviço.

Conhecimentos Obrigatórios:

• Pacote Microsoft Office avançado;

• Domínio em práticas para adoção de medidas de gerenciamento (mediante Inspeções, Auditorias e Acompanhamento de Planos de Ação);&nbsp;

• Apoio na elaboração de Análises Preliminares de Risco (APR), HAZOP (Avaliação de Perigos na Operabilidade de Sistemas) e Análises Quantitativas de Riscos (AQR) de novos empreendimentos ou existentes;&nbsp;

• Experiência consolidada com atividades em plantas industriais;

• Participação em simulados de emergências de grande amplitude em plantas industriais.

Conhecimentos complementares

• Inglês básico;

• Desejável capacitação em sistemas de gestão, HO e/ou ergonomia.

Atribuições

• Realizar inspeções/auditorias;

• Participar e/ou conduzir análises de riscos;

• Realizar análise de anomalias;&nbsp;

• Apoiar atividades relativas a contingências e emergências;&nbsp;

• Apoiar atividades relativas a higiene ocupacional e ergonomia;

• Acompanhar auditorias e visitas de órgãos fiscalizadores;&nbsp;

• Treinar/orientar força de trabalho;

• Apoiar fiscalização de SMS de contratos;

• Coletar e registrar dados em sistemas informatizados;&nbsp;

• Apoiar organização de eventos.

